================================================================================
Current Repository Scope (Milestone 0)
================================================================================

This repository currently contains only the initial project structure, governance
documents, and workflow definitions. No third-party compiled binaries, external
source code modules, or machine learning model weights are bundled or distributed
in this initial repository state.

================================================================================
Planned Third-Party Components and Architectural Dependencies
================================================================================

The architectural design of MTG Collection Manager anticipates extracting,
adapting, or interfacing with the following external third-party components in
future development milestones:

1. Cardloader (Planned extraction in future milestones)
   - Origin: https://github.com/ximilar-com/cardloader
   - Copyright (c) 2024-2026 Ximilar s.r.o.
   - License: Apache License, Version 2.0
   - Planned use: Selected modular components (e.g. TWAIN sidecar and download
     routines) will be evaluated and adapted. When integrated, original copyright
     notices and file-level modification notices will be preserved in the respective
     source files as required by Section 4(b) and 4(c) of Apache-2.0.

2. TWAIN Data Source Manager (Planned runtime dependency on Windows)
   - Origin: https://github.com/twain/twain-dsm
   - Copyright (c) TWAIN Working Group
   - License: GNU Lesser General Public License (LGPL), Version 2.1
   - Planned use: The Windows TWAIN helper sidecar plans to dynamically load
     the official 32-bit TWAINDSM.dll at runtime. The TWAINDSM binary is not
     currently bundled in this repository.

3. llama.cpp (Planned local inference engine)
   - Origin: https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp
   - Copyright (c) 2023-2026 Georgi Gerganov and contributors
   - License: MIT License
   - Planned use: Future integration via Rust bindings (llama-cpp-2) for optional
     local vision-language model inference. Not currently compiled or included.

4. Liquid AI LFM Models (Planned optional user downloads)
   - Origin: https://www.liquid.ai / Hugging Face (LiquidAI)
   - License: LFM Open License v1.0
   - Planned use: Supported as an optional on-demand download initiated directly
     by the user. Model weights are never bundled with this project's source code
     or distributed installers.

